troke-width="1.6"/><text class="ab" y="4.5" text-anchor="middle">13</text></g></g></g></svg><figcaption style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:.6rem">The numbers match the list of places. Map data: U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line; Horry County GIS.</figcaption></figure></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 7, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">From Loris to Pawleys Island: where the sand is closest, where an acre is normal, where builders are selling, and what changes at the city line.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Where to live near Myrtle Beach depends on what you want most. Closest to the sand: Surfside Beach, Garden City and North Myrtle Beach. The most land: Aynor and Loris. The newest houses: Carolina Forest and Longs. The shortest drive to everything: Myrtle Beach and Socastee. The lowest prices: Conway, Loris, Longs and Socastee.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Pick the one or two things that matter most to you. The list below keeps only the places that have them.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Want a short list of towns that fit your budget?</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Have us build your shortlist</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="find-your-town"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Find your town">Which town near Myrtle Beach fits what you want?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each place here leads on something different: the sand, the land, newer houses or a short drive.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A typical house, on this page, is the one in the middle: half sold for more and half for less.</p><div class="c3t-find" id="find"><div class="c3t-chips" role="group" aria-label="What you want" hidden><button type="button" class="c3t-chip" data-k="b1" aria-pressed="false">Up to $300,000</button><button type="button" class="c3t-chip" data-k="b2" aria-pressed="false">$300,000 to $450,000</button><button type="button" class="c3t-chip" data-k="b3" aria-pressed="false">Over $450,000</button><button type="button" class="c3t-chip" data-k="sand" aria-pressed="false">Beach in 10 minutes</button><button type="button" class="c3t-chip" data-k="land" aria-pressed="false">Acre lots common</button><button type="button" class="c3t-chip" data-k="new" aria-pressed="false">Builders selling now</button><button type="button" class="c3t-chip" data-k="dry" aria-pressed="false">Few in a flood zone</button><button type="button" class="c3t-chip" data-k="nohoa" aria-pressed="false">Mostly no HOA fee</button><button type="button" class="c3t-chip" data-k="cost" aria-pressed="false">Lowest yearly cost</button></div><p class="c3t-count" aria-live="polite" hidden></p><p class="c3t-none" hidden>No place has all of these. Remove one choice to see the closest.</p><div class="c3t-tw"><div class="c3t-pick2" hidden><label>Show: <select data-a="data-a"><option value="price" selected>Typical house</option><option value="yearly">Year