7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span>To the beach</dt> <dd>35 min</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span>In a flood zone</dt> <dd>1%</dd></div> </dl><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">More houses for sale here list parking for an RV or a boat than in any other place on this page. Most list no HOA fee. McLeod Health Loris is the nearest hospital for almost every house.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses around Loris sold for about $280,000. A house here also costs the least of any place on this page to keep each year.</p><div class="c3t-act"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Loris">Send me houses in Loris<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><a class="c3t-back" href="#find-your-town">Back to the comparison</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="aynor"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Aynor"><span class="c3t-n">2<span class="c3t-sr">. </span></span><span class="c3t-pn">Aynor</span><span class="c3t-tg"><span class="c3t-sr">: </span>an acre is the usual lot</span></h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Around Aynor, the usual house has about an acre of land, and more than half of house lots are an acre or more. Farm fields start at the edge of the town's grid of streets.</p><div class="c3t-ph"><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-relocating-which-town/aynor-town-and-fields-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-relocating-which-town/aynor-town-and-fields-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/buyers-relocating-which-town/aynor-town-and-fields-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 899px) calc(100vw - 64px), 460px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of Aynor with houses on large grassy lots along a grid of streets on the right, a highway in the middle and plowed farm fields and woods on the left" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo, 2023. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo, 2023</a></span></div><figcaption>Aynor from above: houses on big lots along the town's grid of streets, and farm fields and woods across the highway.</figcaption></figure></div></div><dl class="c3t-kf"><div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span>Typical house</dt> <dd>$350,000</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span>Yearly cost</dt> <dd>$6,600</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span>To the beach</dt> <dd>45 min</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span>In a flood zone</dt> <dd>under 1%</dd></div> </dl><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">State law names the third Saturday in September "Aynor Harvest Hoe-Down Festival Weekend". The Pilot Club of Aynor started the festival in 1979.</p><ul class="c3t-facts" role="list"><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span><span>The trade-off is distance. Aynor is the farthest of these places from the beach, and from a hospital.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Expect about $350,000 for a house around Aynor, the middle of the past year's sales.</p><div class="c3t-act"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Aynor">Send me houses in Aynor<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><a class="c3t-back" href="#find-your-town">Back to the comparison</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="longs"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Longs"><span class="c3t-n">3<span class="c3t-sr">. </span></span><span class="c3t-pn">Longs</span><span class="c3t-tg"><span class="c3t-sr">: </span>where builders are selling</span></h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About half the houses sold in Longs in the past year were new, and about half the houses for sale now are new too.</p><div class="c3t-ph"><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-relocating-which-town/longs-new-subdivision-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-relocating-which-town/longs-new-subdivision-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/buyers-relocating-which-town/longs-new-subdivision-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 899px) calc(100vw - 64px), 460px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of a new subdivision in Longs with streets and ponds cut into bare ground, a few rows of new houses, empty lots, and farm fields and woods around it" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo, 2023. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo, 2023</a></span></div><figcaption>A new subdivision going up beside farm fields in Longs: streets and ponds dug, some houses built or framed, and most lots still empty.</figcaption></figure></div></div><dl class="c3t-kf"><div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span>Typical house</dt> <dd>$300,000</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span>Yearly cost</dt> <dd>$7,700</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span>To the beach</dt> <dd>20 min</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span>In a flood zone</dt> <dd>3%</dd></div> </dl><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For houses for sale with a Longs address, a new house asks about the same price per square foot as one built three to ten years ago.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A Longs mailing address can be inside North Myrtle Beach, as at Grande Dunes North and Waterside, two of the county's ten busiest new communities.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our clients from North Carolina bought land in Longs and had a new house built on it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses in Longs sold for about $300,000, and the usual HOA fee is about $100 a month.</p><div class="c3t-act"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Longs">Send me houses in Longs<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><a class="c3t-back" href="#find-your-town">Back to the comparison</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="little-river"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Little River"><span class="c3t-n">4<span class="c3t-sr">. </span></span><span class="c3t-pn">Little River</span><span class="c3t-tg"><span class="c3t-sr">: </span>old gardens on the waterway, and boat slips</span></h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="/submarkets/little-river/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Little River</a> has a county park on the Intracoastal Waterway: Vereen Memorial Historical Gardens, more than 115 acres of forest and marsh with trails and boardwalks.</p><div class="c3t-ph"><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-little-river/little-river-harbours-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-little-river/little-river-harbours-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-little-river/little-river-harbours-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 899px) calc(100vw - 64px), 460px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A marina basin full of boats off the Intracoastal Waterway, from above, with Coquina Harbour labelled at its upper end, Lightkeepers Village near its mouth, US 17 at the top left and a golf course at the upper right" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo, 2023. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo, 2023</a></span></div><figcaption>Two of Little River's marinas share one basin off the Intracoastal Waterway, with slips sold with their own deed.</figcaption></figure></div></div><dl class="c3t-kf"><div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span>Typical house</dt> <dd>$380,000</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span>Yearly cost</dt> <dd>$8,000</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span>To the beach</dt> <dd>14 min</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span>In a flood zone</dt> <dd>4%</dd></div> </dl><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Boats are the other draw. About 2 in 3 of the county's boat slips sold with their own deed and tax bill are here.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Little River is not a town, so the county makes the rules, and there is no city tax.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Half the houses here sold for more than $380,000, and half for less. Nearly every sale was a resale, not a new house.</p><div class="c3t-act"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Little%20River">Send me houses in Little River<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><a class="c3t-back" href="#find-your-town">Back to the comparison</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="conway"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Conway"><span class="c3t-n">5<span class="c3t-sr">. </span></span><span class="c3t-pn">Conway</span><span class="c3t-tg"><span class="c3t-sr">: </span>a river city with its own services</span></h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="/submarkets/conway/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Conway</a> was laid out in 1732, as Kingston. Its older streets of houses under live oaks run down to the Waccamaw River.</p><div class="c3t-ph"><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/conway-older-house-and-oak-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/conway-older-house-and-oak-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/conway-older-house-and-oak-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 899px) calc(100vw - 64px), 460px" width="1200" height="900" alt="An older white wood house with black shutters behind a large oak tree, with a paved driveway, a low brick planter and thick shrubs, on a shaded street in Conway" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>An older house under a live oak, a few blocks from Main Street in Conway.</figcaption></figure></div></div><dl class="c3t-kf"><div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span>Typical house</dt> <dd>$271,000</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span>Yearly cost</dt> <dd>$7,900</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span>To the beach</dt> <dd>30 min</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span>In a flood zone</dt> <dd>5%</dd></div> </dl><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Riverwalk is a path along the river with benches and a kayak launch. Riverfront Park beside it has a public boat landing with floating docks.</p><ul class="c3t-facts" role="list"><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 3h8l4 4v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H6a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM14 3v4h4M9 17l6-6"/><circle cx="9.5" cy="11.5" r="1"/><circle cx="14.5" cy="16.5" r="1"/></svg></span><span>The city tax is high: about $654 a year on each $100,000 of value, against about $368 outside the towns.</span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span><span>The river reached major flood stage 6 times from 2015 through 2025. About 95 in 100 homes in the city are outside both FEMA's high-risk zone and the land Florence's water reached.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At about $271,000, a typical house in Conway sold for the least of any place here.</p><div class="c3t-act"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Conway">Send me houses in Conway<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><a class="c3t-back" href="#find-your-town">Back to the comparison</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want land, a newer house or a lower tax bill?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us which matters most. We plan a day of showings in two inland towns, so you see both before you choose.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us plan a showing day</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="north-myrtle-beach"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="North Myrtle Beach"><span class="c3t-n">6<span class="c3t-sr">. </span></span><span class="c3t-pn">North Myrtle Beach</span><span class="c3t-tg"><span class="c3t-sr">: </span>most houses for sale near the sand</span></h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 3 in 4 houses for sale in <a href="/submarkets/north-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">North Myrtle Beach</a> are within a mile of the beach. At Cherry Grove, at the north end, about 680 houses sit on dug channels and the marsh edge.</p><div class="c3t-ph"><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/del-webb-north-myrtle-beach/north-myrtle-beach-beach-umbrellas-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/del-webb-north-myrtle-beach/north-myrtle-beach-beach-umbrellas-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/del-webb-north-myrtle-beach/north-myrtle-beach-beach-umbrellas-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 899px) calc(100vw - 64px), 460px" width="1200" height="800" alt="Rows of beach chairs and blue, green and yellow umbrellas on the wide sand beach in North Myrtle Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: JefferyGoldman. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: JefferyGoldman</a></span></div><figcaption>Rows of beach chairs and umbrellas on the wide sand beach in North Myrtle Beach.</figcaption></figure></div></div><dl class="c3t-kf"><div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span>Typical house</dt> <dd>$565,000</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span>Yearly cost</dt> <dd>$7,800</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span>To the beach</dt> <dd>6 min</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span>In a flood zone</dt> <dd>22%</dd></div> </dl><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city's boat ramp at Cherry Grove reaches the ocean through Hog Inlet. Our clients from New York bought beachfront here near the waterway, so they could finally use their boat.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Count on about $565,000 for a typical house. About half the houses for sale list no HOA fee.</p><div class="c3t-act"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=North%20Myrtle%20Beach">Send me houses in North Myrtle Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><a class="c3t-back" href="#find-your-town">Back to the comparison</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="carolina-forest"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Carolina Forest"><span class="c3t-n">7<span class="c3t-sr">. </span></span><span class="c3t-pn">Carolina Forest</span><span class="c3t-tg"><span class="c3t-sr">: </span>the newest homes, almost no flood zone</span></h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Half the homes in <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Carolina Forest</a> were built in 2007 or later, the newest of any place here. Under 1 percent of its houses are in FEMA's high-risk flood zone.</p><div class="c3t-ph"><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-relocating-which-town/carolina-forest-houses-and-woods-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-relocating-which-town/carolina-forest-houses-and-woods-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/buyers-relocating-which-town/carolina-forest-houses-and-woods-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 899px) calc(100vw - 64px), 460px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of a subdivision of houses on cul-de-sac streets in Carolina Forest, with ponds, thick woods around it and cleared land on the right" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo, 2023. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo, 2023</a></span></div><figcaption>Houses on streets that end in cul-de-sacs in Carolina Forest, with woods around them and land being cleared for more on the right.</figcaption></figure></div></div><dl class="c3t-kf"><div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span>Typical house</dt> <dd>$440,000</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span>Yearly cost</dt> <dd>$8,500</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span>To the beach</dt> <dd>20 min</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span>In a flood zone</dt> <dd>under 1%</dd></div> </dl><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It is a large planned area of neighborhoods outside the city limits. McLeod Health cut the ribbon on a new hospital here in August 2026. The county's Bike and Run Park, on the waterway, has miles of mountain bike and hiking trails.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Nearly every house for sale in the Carolina Forest ZIP code lists an HOA fee, about $125 a month in a typical listing.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The middle sale here in the past year was about $440,000.</p><div class="c3t-act"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Carolina%20Forest">Send me houses in Carolina Forest<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><a class="c3t-back" href="#find-your-town">Back to the comparison</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="myrtle-beach"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Myrtle Beach"><span class="c3t-n">8<span class="c3t-sr">. </span></span><span class="c3t-pn">Myrtle Beach</span><span class="c3t-tg"><span class="c3t-sr">: </span>the shortest drive to everything</span></h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From a typical house in <a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach</a>, the beach, the airport and Coastal Grand Mall are each about 15 minutes or less by car.</p><div class="c3t-ph"><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-buying-in-myrtle-beach/myrtle-beach-skywheel-beach-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-buying-in-myrtle-beach/myrtle-beach-skywheel-beach-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/buyers-buying-in-myrtle-beach/myrtle-beach-skywheel-beach-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 899px) calc(100vw - 64px), 460px" width="1200" height="675" alt="The wide beach in downtown Myrtle Beach at low tide, with the SkyWheel, rows of blue umbrellas and towers along the shore" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Tom Long, CC BY-SA 2.0. License: CC BY-SA 2.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 2.0">Photo: Tom Long, CC BY-SA 2.0</a></span></div><figcaption>The beach in downtown Myrtle Beach at low tide, seen from a pier, with the SkyWheel behind it.</figcaption></figure></div></div><dl class="c3t-kf"><div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span>Typical house</dt> <dd>$535,000</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span>Yearly cost</dt> <dd>$8,600</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span>To the beach</dt> <dd>10 min</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span>In a flood zone</dt> <dd>5%</dd></div> </dl><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Market Common is a town center with shops, restaurants and a movie theater, and apartments above the stores.</p><ul class="c3t-facts" role="list"><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V9.5l5-3V21M10 21V4h9v17M13 8h3M13 12h3M13 16h3M7.5 13h.01M7.5 16.5h.01"/></svg></span><span>A city resident's parking decal costs nothing, and it covers parking at the city's meters and pay stations.</span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span>Nearly every house in the city is outside the zones that allow rentals under 90 days.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the city, houses sold for about $535,000 at the middle of the past year.</p><div class="c3t-act"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Myrtle%20Beach">Send me houses in Myrtle Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><a class="c3t-back" href="#find-your-town">Back to the comparison</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Is the house you like inside the city?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We tell you which side of the city line it is on, and what that changes.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask us about an address</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="socastee"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Socastee"><span class="c3t-n">9<span class="c3t-sr">. </span></span><span class="c3t-pn">Socastee</span><span class="c3t-tg"><span class="c3t-sr">: </span>a historic village on the waterway</span></h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Socastee began in the late 1800s as a lumber and turpentine camp. Its old swing bridge, built in the mid-1930s, carries Dick Pond Road over the Intracoastal Waterway. The bridge, two houses, a store and a pecan grove make up a historic district on the National Register.</p><div class="c3t-ph"><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-relocating-which-town/socastee-swing-bridge-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-relocating-which-town/socastee-swing-bridge-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/buyers-relocating-which-town/socastee-swing-bridge-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 899px) calc(100vw - 64px), 460px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of a blue steel truss swing bridge carrying a two-lane road over the Intracoastal Waterway at Socastee, with a newer four-lane bridge at the lower left and houses at the upper left" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo, 2023. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo, 2023</a></span></div><figcaption>The old Socastee swing bridge, the blue steel span, on the Intracoastal Waterway, with the newer highway bridge at the lower left.</figcaption></figure></div></div><dl class="c3t-kf"><div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span>Typical house</dt> <dd>$300,000</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span>Yearly cost</dt> <dd>$7,700</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span>To the beach</dt> <dd>13 min</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span>In a flood zone</dt> <dd>11%</dd></div> </dl><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house here costs about what it does in Longs, but Socastee is much closer to the beach and the airport.</p><ul class="c3t-facts" role="list"><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span><span>About 1 in 9 houses here are in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, more than twice the share in Conway or Myrtle Beach. We check the zone for each house.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A typical house in Socastee costs about $300,000.</p><div class="c3t-act"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Socastee">Send me houses in Socastee<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><a class="c3t-back" href="#find-your-town">Back to the comparison</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="surfside-beach"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Surfside Beach"><span class="c3t-n">10<span class="c3t-sr">. </span></span><span class="c3t-pn">Surfside Beach</span><span class="c3t-tg"><span class="c3t-sr">: </span>the sand at the end of the street</span></h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In <a href="/submarkets/surfside-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Surfside Beach</a>, a typical house is about 3 minutes by car from the sand, the closest of any place here. Every home in the town is less than a mile from Ocean Boulevard, the beach road.</p><div class="c3t-ph"><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/surfside-beach-houses-from-the-sand-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/surfside-beach-houses-from-the-sand-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/surfside-beach-houses-from-the-sand-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 899px) calc(100vw - 64px), 460px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A row of two- and three-story beach houses in blue, yellow and gray behind low dunes, seen across a wide sand beach under a blue sky at Surfside Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: BullDawg2021. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: BullDawg2021</a></span></div><figcaption>Beach houses in a row behind the dunes at Surfside Beach, seen from the sand.</figcaption></figure></div></div><dl class="c3t-kf"><div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span>Typical house</dt> <dd>$705,000</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span>Yearly cost</dt> <dd>$8,300</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span>To the beach</dt> <dd>3 min</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span>In a flood zone</dt> <dd>30%</dd></div> </dl><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Along the ocean, only about 1 in 8 homes here is taxed as someone's main home.</p><ul class="c3t-facts" role="list"><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span><span>About 3 in 10 houses here are inside FEMA's high-risk flood zone, so we check each one.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At about $705,000, a typical house here sold for the most of any place on this page.</p><div class="c3t-act"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Surfside%20Beach">Send me houses in Surfside Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><a class="c3t-back" href="#find-your-town">Back to the comparison</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Found a house near the beach?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the house. We check its flood zone and what a flood policy costs there before you make an offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us check the flood zone</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="garden-city"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Garden City"><span class="c3t-n">11<span class="c3t-sr">. </span></span><span class="c3t-pn">Garden City</span><span class="c3t-tg"><span class="c3t-sr">: </span>between the ocean and the marsh</span></h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="/submarkets/garden-city/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Garden City</a> is a strip of beach houses between the ocean and the salt marsh. Its pier is 668 feet long, with bands every night at both ends, weather permitting.</p><div class="c3t-ph"><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 899px) calc(100vw - 64px), 460px" width="1200" height="782" alt="Beach houses in rows between the ocean beach and a wide marsh with tidal creeks and boat docks at Garden City Beach, seen from a plane over the ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Beach houses at Garden City, seen from over the ocean, with the salt marsh and its creeks behind them.</figcaption></figure></div></div><dl class="c3t-kf"><div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span>Typical house</dt> <dd>$406,000</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span>Yearly cost</dt> <dd>$8,200</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span>To the beach</dt> <dd>5 min</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span>In a flood zone</dt> <dd>31%</dd></div> </dl><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From November through February, the county lets golf carts drive on its beach here, with a state permit and a licensed driver.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses in Garden City sold for about $406,000 at the middle, about $300,000 less than in Surfside Beach, the next place north.</p><div class="c3t-act"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Garden%20City">Send me houses in Garden City<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><a class="c3t-back" href="#find-your-town">Back to the comparison</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="murrells-inlet"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Murrells Inlet"><span class="c3t-n">12<span class="c3t-sr">. </span></span><span class="c3t-pn">Murrells Inlet</span><span class="c3t-tg"><span class="c3t-sr">: </span>the creek and the closest hospital</span></h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The <a href="/submarkets/murrells-inlet/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Murrells Inlet</a> on this page is the part in Georgetown County, south of the county line. Houses on the creek side of Business 17 have docks over the marsh.</p><div class="c3t-ph"><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/murrells-inlet-boats-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/murrells-inlet-boats-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/murrells-inlet-boats-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 899px) calc(100vw - 64px), 460px" width="1200" height="759" alt="White fishing boats tied up at a marina on calm water in Murrells Inlet, South Carolina" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pollinator. License: CC BY-SA 3.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 3.0">Photo: Pollinator</a></span></div><figcaption>Fishing boats tied up at a marina in Murrells Inlet.</figcaption></figure></div></div><dl class="c3t-kf"><div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span>Typical house</dt> <dd>$610,000</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span>Yearly cost</dt> <dd>$9,700</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span>To the beach</dt> <dd>10 min</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span>In a flood zone</dt> <dd>18%</dd></div> </dl><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The MarshWalk is a half-mile wooden boardwalk along the marsh, with restaurants and free live music. A hospital is about 6 minutes from a typical house, the closest of any place here.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The middle sale here was about $610,000. Of all 13 places, Murrells Inlet has the highest yearly cost to keep a house.</p><div class="c3t-act"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Murrells%20Inlet">Send me houses in Murrells Inlet<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><a class="c3t-back" href="#find-your-town">Back to the comparison</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="pawleys-litchfield"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pawleys Island"><span class="c3t-n">13<span class="c3t-sr">. </span></span><span class="c3t-pn">Pawleys Island and Litchfield</span><span class="c3t-tg"><span class="c3t-sr">: </span>an island town where houses rarely sell</span></h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Town of <a href="/submarkets/pawleys-island/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Pawleys Island</a> is the island itself, a town of its own since 1985. The mainland around it with a Pawleys Island address is county land, and so is Litchfield.</p><div class="c3t-ph"><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/pawleys-island-beach-walkway-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/pawleys-island-beach-walkway-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/pawleys-island-beach-walkway-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 899px) calc(100vw - 64px), 460px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A wooden walkway over green dunes leading to the ocean on Pawleys Island" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Phoebe. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: Phoebe</a></span></div><figcaption>A wooden walkway over the dunes to the beach on Pawleys Island.</figcaption></figure></div></div><dl class="c3t-kf"><div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span>Typical house</dt> <dd>$650,000</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span>Yearly cost</dt> <dd>$9,500</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span>To the beach</dt> <dd>7 min</dd></div> <div><dt><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span>In a flood zone</dt> <dd>32%</dd></div> </dl><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The island has about 480 houses, and they rarely sell: only 10 changed hands at a market price in the past year. Every island house but one is in FEMA's high-risk flood zone.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Across the island, the mainland and Litchfield, the middle sale was about $650,000, and nearly all of those sales were off the island. On the island itself, the middle sale over the last three years was about $2.45 million.</p><div class="c3t-act"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Pawleys%20Island">Send me houses in Pawleys Island<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><a class="c3t-back" href="#find-your-town">Back to the comparison</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="compare"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Compare">How do the towns compare on price and the cost to keep a house?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:72