aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $8,300 a year</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$705,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">13. Pawleys Island</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $9,500 a year</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.922" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$650,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">12. Murrells Inlet</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $9,700 a year</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.865" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$610,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">6. North Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $7,800 a year</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.801" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$565,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">8. Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $8,600 a year</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.759" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$535,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">7. Carolina Forest</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $8,500 a year</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.624" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$440,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">11. Garden City</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $8,200 a year</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.575" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$406,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">4. Little River</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $8,000 a year</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.539" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$380,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2. Aynor</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $6,600 a year</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.493" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$350,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">3. Longs</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $7,700 a year</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.425" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$300,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">9. Socastee</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $7,700 a year</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.425" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$300,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1. Loris</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $6,400 a year</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.397" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$280,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">5. Conway</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $7,900 a year</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.384" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$271,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Detached houses, not condos or townhouses, sold in the year to September 2026. The cost each year is for a house you live in, outside the flood zone: the tax, the county fee, insurance, the HOA fee and upkeep.</figcaption></figure><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Narrowed it to two or three?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us which places and your budget. We send houses for sale there, with the flood zone, the tax and the HOA fee for each.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Send us your towns</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly cost">What does a house cost to keep each year besides the mortgage?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a typical house, about $6,400 to $9,700 a year, as your home and outside the flood zone. That spread is much smaller than the spread in price.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Take two places. A typical house in North Myrtle Beach sold for nearly twice what one in Longs did. Each year it costs only about $140 more to keep.</p><div class="c3t-ex"><div><h3>Longs</h3><p class="s">Typical house: about $300,000</p><dl><dt>Tax, as your home</dt><dd>$1,100</dd><dt>County fee</dt><dd>$89</dd><dt>Insurance</dt><dd>$2,000</dd><dt>HOA fee</dt><dd>$1,200</dd><dt>Upkeep</dt><dd>$3,300</dd><dt class="t">Total a year</dt><dd class="t">$7,700</dd></dl></div><div><h3>North Myrtle Beach</h3><p class="s">Typical house: about $565,000</p><dl><dt>Tax, as your home</dt><dd>$2,530</dd><dt>County fee</dt><dd>none</dd><dt>Insurance</dt><dd>$2,000</dd><dt>HOA fee</dt><dd>none</dd><dt>Upkeep</dt><dd>$3,300</dd><dt class="t">Total a year</dt><dd class="t">$7,800</dd></dl></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Near the beach, insurance and flood insurance can widen the gap. A typical Surfside Beach house in the high-risk flood zone, with a $3,000 insurance bill, costs about $10,400 a year instead of $8,300. Our <a href="/buyers/cost-to-own/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">cost to own</a> page breaks down every part.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want the yearly cost of one house?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us a house you like. We work out its tax, its HOA fee, its flood zone and its insurance quotes before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us price a house's yearly cost</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="city-or-county"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="City or county">What changes when a house is inside city limits?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The tax rate, the trash pickup, the sales tax and the rules for rentals and golf carts. Four of the 13 places are a city or town in full. Myrtle Beach, North Myrtle Beach and Conway are cities, and Surfside Beach is a town. The City of Loris, the Town of Aynor and the Town of Pawleys Island sit inside places that are mostly county land.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=row]{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;column-gap:.8rem;align-items:start}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .b{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .dot{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .f{display:block}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=cell]{justify-content:flex-end}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact c3-gchart-list"><div role="table" aria-label="Property tax a year on each $100,000 of value, on a home you live in"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Property tax a year on each $100,000 of value, on a home you live in</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Where the house is, fee on the bill</span><span role="columnheader">tax a year</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Outside the towns, Horry County</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">plus a fee of about $89 on most bills</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.531" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$368</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Garden City</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">plus a fee of about $89 on most bills</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.567" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$393</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">no county fee</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.583" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$404</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Surfside Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">plus an $82 fee</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.607" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$420</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">no county fee</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.648" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$448</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pawleys Island and Litchfield</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">plus a $96 or $44 fee</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.659" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$456</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Murrells Inlet</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">plus a $96 fee</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.745" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$516</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Conway</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">no county fee</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.944" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$654</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">City of Loris</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">no county fee</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$692</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Horry County's tax rates and bills for 2026. Pawleys Island, Litchfield and Murrells Inlet: Georgetown County's current estimate. Before the tax break at 65, below the chart.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At 65, after a year living in South Carolina, the <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">first $50,000 of your home's value</a> is not taxed.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>What changes at the city line</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">What changes</th><th scope="col">Inside a city or town</th><th scope="col">Outside, in the county</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Trash and recycling</th><td data-label="Inside a city or town">The town's service, where it has one</td><td data-label="Outside, in the county">Horry: a hauler or drop-off center</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sales tax</th><td data-label="Inside a city or town">9% Myrtle Beach; 8% Horry; 7% Pawleys</td><td data-label="Outside, in the county">8% in Horry, 7% in Georgetown</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Renting by the night</th><td data-label="Inside a city or town">Each town's own rule</td><td data-label="Outside, in the county">Horry: no limit. Georgetown: one zone</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Golf cart hours and streets</th><td data-label="Inside a city or town">Each town can set its own</td><td data-label="Outside, in the county">The county's rules, or the state's</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Renting by the night: in Myrtle Beach most neighborhoods of houses are not zoned for stays under 90 days. North Myrtle Beach needs only a yearly business license and the lodging taxes. Surfside Beach allows stays under 30 days only in the zoning districts along the ocean. Conway allows them in three downtown districts.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Outside the towns, Horry County has no curb pickup, only 25 drop-off centers for residents.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A subdivision's recorded rules can bar nightly rentals even where zoning allows them. Our <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">rental rules</a> page has each town's rule in full.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want the rules for one address?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us what you plan to do with the house. We read the town's rules and the HOA's recorded rules for that address.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask us to check the rules</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="questions-about-the-towns"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Questions about the towns</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is it better to live in Myrtle Beach or North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A typical house costs about the same in both: $535,000 in Myrtle Beach and $565,000 in North Myrtle Beach. In North Myrtle Beach it is closer to the beach, but more often in the high-risk flood zone. Myrtle Beach is much closer to the airport, and most of its neighborhoods of houses are not zoned for nightly rentals.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does a Myrtle Beach address mean the house is in the city?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not always. Carolina Forest houses, and many in Socastee, have Myrtle Beach mailing addresses but are outside the city limits. They pay no city tax and get no city trash pickup.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Where near Myrtle Beach are most houses someone's home all year?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In most of these places, about 3 in 4 houses or more are the owner's main home, taxed at the 4 percent rate. In North Myrtle Beach about half are, and in Surfside Beach fewer than half. The rest are taxed at the 6 percent rate for second homes and rentals.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which town near Myrtle Beach has the least crime?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Chapter3 does not rate any town on crime or describe who lives anywhere. Fair housing law bars agents from steering buyers toward or away from an area. We give you the record of the house itself: its flood zone, its tax and the rules for its address.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/search/SearchTypeDocType" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry deeds</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry parcels</a>, <a href="https://gis1.georgetowncountysc.org/portal/home/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Georgetown parcels</a>, <a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/home" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood maps</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/nfip-redacted-policies-v3" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA policies</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry 2026 levy</a>, <a href="https://www.gtcountysc.gov/385/Property-Tax-Calculator" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Georgetown tax</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table/ACSDT5Y2024.B25035" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census ACS</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/sites/dor/files/forms/ST500.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOR ST-500</a>, <a href="https://www.solidwasteauthority.org/recyclingcenters.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Solid Waste Authority</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t56c002.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 56-2</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/services/parking_meters/index.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtle Beach parking</a>, <a href="https://projectportal.scdot.org/sc-historic-bridges/s-616-bridge-over-intercoastal-waterway-horry-county" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOT bridge record</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/parksandrecreation/parks" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry parks</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c037.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-37</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t38c075.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 38-75</a>. Prices: recorded sales of detached houses, not values. Drives: OpenStreetMap roads, 60 random houses per place. Card insurance: the Horry County middle. Longs: outside North Myrtle Beach. Listings: our feed, in aggregate.</p><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Main Street in downtown Loris, with brick shop buildings on both sides. Photo: Pithon314, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Downtown_Loris,_South_Carolina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>. Chapter3 Realty cropped this photo to the street and the shops, leaving out the sky and the traffic lights, and resized it.</div><div role="listitem">Aynor from above: houses on big lots along the town's grid of streets, and farm fields and woods across the highway. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>.</div><div role="listitem">A new subdivision going up beside farm fields in Longs: streets and ponds dug, some houses built or framed, and most lots still empty. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Two of Little River's marinas share one basin off the Intracoastal Waterway, with slips sold with their own deed. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service 